  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Collective Initiatives RISE (Refugee Integration through Support and Employment)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to to assess the barriers and ways forward for refugees from Ukraine to access sustainable livelihood opportunities in Poland, through employment or through running their own businesses. The analysis will involve a range of quantitative and qualitative research activities while taking gendered considerations and the perspectives of marginalized and disadvantaged groups of refugees into consideration. Through this research, the IRC and Save the Children Poland intend to bring together perspectives from the self-entrepreneurs, local and multinational businesses, and job seekers communities, in order to connect, triangulate, and consolidate elements of knowledge that are currently siloed and separated in the existing literature and research ecosystem.</narrative>
  </description>
